# USB fix: adbd only ships on this device as the flattened com.android.adbd APEX
# (/system/apex/com.android.adbd/bin/adbd) - there is no plain /system/bin/adbd fallback in the
# system build (confirmed absent from target-files; the platform's own service definition in
# system/core/rootdir/init.usb.rc is "disabled"+"updatable" and only gets a real backing binary
# if apexd successfully activates that APEX during early boot and injects an override from
# /apex/com.android.adbd/etc/init.rc). Every USB config trigger in init.usb(.configfs).rc that
# does "start adbd" silently no-ops if that activation never happened, sys.usb.ffs.ready never
# becomes 1, and the UDC (see init.usb.configfs.rc) is never written - the host sees literally
# nothing, matching the observed symptom exactly. Remove the apexd dependency from the chain
# entirely: redefine the "adbd" service (same name, so every existing "start adbd" trigger
# elsewhere picks this up automatically - no other file needs to change) to exec the flattened
# binary directly, a plain file guaranteed available as soon as /system is mounted. `override`
# is the standard init mechanism for a later-parsed vendor/device file replacing an
# earlier-parsed platform service definition (vendor's init directory is parsed after /system's).
service adbd /system/apex/com.android.adbd/bin/adbd --root_seclabel=u:r:su:s0
    class core
    socket adbd seqpacket 660 system system
    disabled
    seclabel u:r:adbd:s0
    override
